msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow job works like a batch job on an HPC compute node. The job's local disk is scratch space. The job can write to it, but the workflow deletes it when the job ends. To keep files after the job ends, save them to file storage, which works like your own storage bucket. Files that you upload, and files that your workflow saves, remain in file storage, and later runs of the workflow can read them.\n"
msgstr "Tugas aliran kerja terurus berfungsi seperti tugas kelompok pada nod pengiraan HPC. Cakera setempat tugas ialah ruang calar. Tugas boleh menulis padanya, tetapi aliran kerja memadamnya apabila tugas tamat. Untuk mengekalkan fail selepas tugas tamat, simpannya ke storan fail, yang berfungsi seperti baldi storan anda sendiri. Fail yang anda muat naik, dan fail yang disimpan oleh aliran kerja anda, kekal dalam storan fail, dan larian aliran kerja kemudian boleh membacanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each workflow has its own file storage for each user. Other users who run the same workflow do not see your files.\n"
msgstr "Setiap aliran kerja mempunyai storan failnya sendiri bagi setiap pengguna. Pengguna lain yang menjalankan aliran kerja yang sama tidak melihat fail anda.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![File storage for the workflow sits at the center. Your local notebook reaches it with the client file methods file_upload(), files(), file_download(), and file_delete(). File storage is yours only, because other users of the workflow do not see your files. It is kept after each job ends and is shared by all of your runs, and a file with the same name replaces the earlier file. Each job sees file storage as the folder /function_user_data. Run 1 also has a local disk at /tmp, which is deleted when the job ends, and copies finished files from /tmp to /function_user_data. Run 2 reads the files that earlier runs saved.](/docs/images/managed-workflows/manage-files.svg)\n"
msgstr "![File storage for the workflow sits at the center. Your local notebook reaches it with the client file methods file_upload(), files(), file_download(), and file_delete(). File storage is yours only, because other users of the workflow do not see your files. It is kept after each job ends and is shared by all of your runs, and a file with the same name replaces the earlier file. Each job sees file storage as the folder /function_user_data. Run 1 also has a local disk at /tmp, which is deleted when the job ends, and copies finished files from /tmp to /function_user_data. Run 2 reads the files that earlier runs saved.](/docs/images/managed-workflows/manage-files.svg)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload an input file {#upload-an-input-file}"
msgstr "Muat naik fail input {#upload-an-input-file}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload a file from your local notebook with `file_upload()`, and then list the files in storage with `files()`:\n"
msgstr "Muat naik fail daripada buku nota setempat anda dengan `file_upload()`, kemudian senaraikan fail dalam storan dengan `files()`:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr "**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the gateway sets no size limit for uploaded files (gateway/main/settings.py, specs/ARGUMENTS_LIMIT.md). The Helm ingress sets proxy-body-size to 50m. Confirm the limit in production. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Supported file types {#supported-file-types}"
msgstr "Jenis fail yang disokong {#supported-file-types}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow checks the contents of each uploaded file, not its extension, and rejects files of other types:\n"
msgstr "Aliran kerja terurus menyemak kandungan setiap fail yang dimuat naik, bukan sambungannya, dan menolak fail jenis lain:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Accepted | Rejected |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| JSON, plain text, YAML, and Python files; binary files such as NumPy (`.npy`, `.npz`), QPY, and pickle files; tar, gzip, and zip archives | CSV, PNG, PDF, HDF5, and empty files |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Diterima | Ditolak |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| Fail JSON, teks biasa, YAML dan Python; fail binari seperti NumPy (`.npy`, `.npz`), QPY dan pickle; arkib tar, gzip dan zip | Fail CSV, PNG, PDF, HDF5 dan fail kosong |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: let's figure out if this is recent, and what the file size limitation actually is (50 MB?) */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "File names {#file-names}"
msgstr "Nama fail {#file-names}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Use only letters, digits, underscores (`_`), hyphens (`-`), and periods (`.`).** A managed workflow removes other characters, such as spaces, from the name when you download or delete a file. For example, you can upload `my results.json`, but you cannot download it.\n"
msgstr "**Gunakan hanya huruf, digit, garis bawah (`_`), tanda sempang (`-`), dan noktah (`.`).** Aliran kerja terurus membuang aksara lain, seperti ruang, daripada nama apabila anda memuat turun atau memadam fail. Contohnya, anda boleh memuat naik `my results.json`, tetapi anda tidak boleh memuat turunnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**File storage has no folders.** `file_upload()` keeps only the file name, so `inputs/params.json` is stored as `params.json`.\n"
msgstr "**Storan fail tidak mempunyai folder.** `file_upload()` hanya mengekalkan nama fail, jadi `inputs/params.json` disimpan sebagai `params.json`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: upload does not sanitize file names, but download and delete do (gateway/api/utils.py sanitize_file_name()). Confirm whether upload should reject or sanitize these names. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read files in a workflow {#read-files-in-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Baca fail dalam aliran kerja {#read-files-in-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pass the name of the file when you run the workflow:\n"
msgstr "Hantar nama fail apabila anda menjalankan aliran kerja:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, edit your workflow code to read the file from `/function_user_data`, which is where every job sees file storage:\n"
msgstr "Untuk membolehkan ini, edit kod aliran kerja anda untuk membaca fail daripada `/function_user_data`, iaitu tempat setiap tugas melihat storan fail:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inside a job, read and write files through this folder. The client file methods, such as `file_upload()` and `file_download()`, are for your local notebook.\n"
msgstr "Di dalam tugas, baca dan tulis fail melalui folder ini. Kaedah fail klien, seperti `file_upload()` dan `file_download()`, adalah untuk buku nota setempat anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To read an archive, extract it to the local disk:\n"
msgstr "Untuk membaca arkib, ekstraknya ke cakera setempat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write temporary files to `/tmp`. File storage is object storage that the job sees as a folder, so file storage is slower than the local disk. Do heavy reads and writes on the local disk, and copy finished files to file storage.\n"
msgstr "Tulis fail sementara ke `/tmp`. Storan fail ialah storan objek yang dilihat oleh tugas sebagai folder, jadi storan fail lebih perlahan daripada cakera setempat. Lakukan bacaan dan tulisan yang berat pada cakera setempat, dan salin fail yang siap ke storan fail.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm how the mount behaves for appends, renames, and partial writes, and how soon a file that one job writes is visible to a job that is running at the same time. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Save output files {#save-output-files}"
msgstr "Simpan fail output {#save-output-files}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Your local notebook reads the names of the output files from the result:\n"
msgstr "Buku nota setempat anda membaca nama fail output daripada hasil:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, save each output file at the top level of `/function_user_data`, and return the file names with `save_result()`:\n"
msgstr "Untuk membolehkan ini, simpan setiap fail output pada peringkat teratas `/function_user_data`, dan kembalikan nama fail dengan `save_result()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Files that the job writes outside `/function_user_data`, such as in `/tmp` or the current folder, are deleted when the job ends.\n"
msgstr "Fail yang ditulis oleh tugas di luar `/function_user_data`, seperti dalam `/tmp` atau folder semasa, dipadamkan apabila tugas tamat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: confirm that the mount stores /function_user_data/<folder>/<file> as the storage key .../data/<folder>/<file>, so that later jobs can read subfolders. file_download() can't fetch these files: sanitize_file_name() strips \"/\", and files() lists only the base name (file_storage_fleets.py get_public_files()). */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download output files {#download-output-files}"
msgstr "Muat turun fail output {#download-output-files}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After the job ends, download each file with `file_download()`. Set `target_name` to choose the local file name, and `download_location` to choose an existing local folder:\n"
msgstr "Selepas tugas tamat, muat turun setiap fail dengan `file_download()`. Tetapkan `target_name` untuk memilih nama fail setempat, dan `download_location` untuk memilih folder setempat sedia ada:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Without `target_name`, `file_download()` adds a random prefix to the local file name, such as `downloaded_3f2a9c1b_energies.npy`, and returns the name that it used.\n"
msgstr "Tanpa `target_name`, `file_download()` menambah awalan rawak pada nama fail setempat, seperti `downloaded_3f2a9c1b_energies.npy`, dan mengembalikan nama yang digunakannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Download many outputs as one archive {#download-many-outputs-as-one-archive}"
msgstr "Muat turun banyak output sebagai satu arkib {#download-many-outputs-as-one-archive}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a job saves many output files, or files in subfolders, bundle them into one archive in the workflow, and download only the archive:\n"
msgstr "Jika tugas menyimpan banyak fail output, atau fail dalam subfolder, himpunkannya ke dalam satu arkib dalam aliran kerja, dan muat turun arkib sahaja:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To enable this, write the outputs to a folder on the local disk, add the folder to an archive in `/tmp`, and copy the archive to file storage:\n"
msgstr "Untuk membolehkan ini, tulis output ke folder pada cakera setempat, tambahkan folder itu ke arkib dalam `/tmp`, dan salin arkib ke storan fail:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the archive is built on the local disk and copied in one step, file storage never holds an incomplete archive. The archive keeps the folder structure, and it can contain files of any type. In this example, the files are extracted to `outputs/<run_name>/`.\n"
msgstr "Oleh sebab arkib dibina pada cakera setempat dan disalin dalam satu langkah, storan fail tidak pernah mengandungi arkib yang tidak lengkap. Arkib mengekalkan struktur folder, dan ia boleh mengandungi fail jenis apa pun. Dalam contoh ini, fail diekstrak ke `outputs/<run_name>/`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Delete files {#delete-files}"
msgstr "Padam fail {#delete-files}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow does not delete files from file storage, so files remain until you delete them with `file_delete()`:\n"
msgstr "Aliran kerja terurus tidak memadam fail daripada storan fail, jadi fail kekal sehingga anda memadamnya dengan `file_delete()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`file_delete()` reports success even if the file does not exist, so check the name with `files()` first. To delete all the files of one run, filter `files()` by the run's name prefix, as described in the next section:\n"
msgstr "`file_delete()` melaporkan kejayaan walaupun fail tidak wujud, jadi semak nama dengan `files()` terlebih dahulu. Untuk memadam semua fail satu larian, tapis `files()` mengikut awalan nama larian, seperti yang diterangkan dalam bahagian seterusnya:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: on Fleets, deleting a missing file returns \"Requested file was deleted.\" because gateway/core/ibm_cloud/cos/cos_client.py delete_object() treats a missing key as deleted. Confirm whether file_delete() should return 404 instead. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: give each run's files a unique name {#best-practice-give-each-runs-files-a-unique-name}"
msgstr "Amalan terbaik: beri setiap fail larian nama yang unik {#best-practice-give-each-runs-files-a-unique-name}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All of your runs of a workflow share the same file storage, and a file that a job saves replaces any stored file with the same name. If you start several runs at the same time and each run saves `energies.npy`, only the last one is kept.\n"
msgstr "Semua larian aliran kerja anda berkongsi storan fail yang sama, dan fail yang disimpan oleh sesuatu job menggantikan mana-mana fail tersimpan yang bernama sama. Jika anda memulakan beberapa larian serentak dan setiap larian menyimpan `energies.npy`, hanya yang terakhir dikekalkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a best practice, pass a run name as an argument, and start the name of every file that the run saves with it:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai amalan terbaik, hantar nama larian sebagai argumen, dan mulakan nama setiap fail yang disimpan oleh larian itu dengannya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All runs can read the same input file, `hamiltonian.npz`, because they only read it. Upload a shared input one time, before you start the runs.\n"
msgstr "Semua larian boleh membaca fail input yang sama, `hamiltonian.npz`, kerana mereka hanya membacanya. Muat naik input kongsi sekali sahaja, sebelum anda memulakan larian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use run names that you can recognize later, and that contain only letters, digits, underscores, hyphens, and periods. With one prefix for each run, you can find, download, and [delete](#delete-files) the files of a run together.\n"
msgstr "Gunakan nama larian yang boleh anda kenali kemudian, dan yang hanya mengandungi huruf, digit, garis bawah, tanda sempang dan noktah. Dengan satu awalan bagi setiap larian, anda boleh mencari, memuat turun dan [memadam](#delete-files) fail sesuatu larian bersama-sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Best practice: checkpoint long jobs {#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs}"
msgstr "Amalan terbaik: buat titik semak untuk job yang panjang {#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A job that is canceled, fails, or reaches the 24-hour limit loses everything that is not in file storage. For long runs, save a checkpoint to file storage at regular intervals, and resume from it when you run the workflow again with the same run name:\n"
msgstr "Job yang dibatalkan, gagal atau mencapai had 24 jam kehilangan segala-galanya yang tidak berada dalam storan fail. Untuk larian yang panjang, simpan titik semak ke storan fail pada sela masa tetap, dan sambung semula daripadanya apabila anda menjalankan aliran kerja sekali lagi dengan nama larian yang sama:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To continue a run that stopped, call `run()` again with the same arguments.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menyambung larian yang telah berhenti, panggil `run()` sekali lagi dengan argumen yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the following points in mind:\n"
msgstr "Ingat perkara berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Write the checkpoint to the local disk first, and then copy it.** If the job stops during a write, the stored checkpoint is incomplete, and the next run cannot read it.\n"
msgstr "**Tulis titik semak ke cakera setempat dahulu, kemudian salinnya.** Jika job berhenti semasa penulisan, titik semak yang disimpan tidak lengkap, dan larian seterusnya tidak dapat membacanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Choose an interval that matches the cost of a step.** Save often enough that you do not lose much work, but not so often that writing checkpoints slows the job.\n"
msgstr "**Pilih sela masa yang sepadan dengan kos satu langkah.** Simpan cukup kerap supaya anda tidak kehilangan banyak kerja, tetapi tidak terlalu kerap sehingga penulisan titik semak melambatkan job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Delete checkpoints after the run succeeds.** A later run with the same name then starts from the beginning.\n"
msgstr "**Padam titik semak selepas larian berjaya.** Larian kemudian dengan nama yang sama akan bermula dari awal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a job that is canceled, you can also save partial results in a [`SIGTERM` handler](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"
msgstr "Bagi job yang dibatalkan, anda juga boleh menyimpan keputusan separa dalam [pengendali `SIGTERM`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah seterusnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Run a parameter sweep](/guides/run-parameter-sweep) to start one job for each input.\n"
"- [Write logs and handle errors](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors) to save partial results when a job is canceled.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Cadangan\">\n"
"- [Jalankan penyapuan parameter](/guides/run-parameter-sweep) untuk memulakan satu job bagi setiap input.\n"
"- [Tulis log dan kendalikan ralat](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors) untuk menyimpan keputusan separa apabila job dibatalkan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
